  "answer": "Sales should use the **Corpus Readiness Checklist** (also referred to as the Mandatory Pre-Onboarding Format Audit) before committing to enterprise deployment dates. This checklist is designed to flag data format risks that directly drive deployment delays.\n\n- Sales must require Enterprise prospects to submit a sample of 20 core documents for format analysis during the sales discovery phase. If scanned PDFs are detected, sales must flag this early so the Customer Success team can adjust the target timeline [NL-031#NL-031-S06].\n- The checklist specifically highlights scanned PDF and OCR requirements to manage customer expectations about the standard 8-to-10 week Enterprise implementation timeline [NL-023#NL-023-S07].\n- When a customer has thousands of scanned, image-only PDFs, sales must explicitly tell them that onboarding will be delayed unless they run OCR on their end first (or wait for the upcoming automated OCR pipeline) [NL-015#NL-015-S04].\n- In addition to the corpus checklist, sales must not guarantee specific launch dates for future modules or integrations (e.g., Microsoft Teams) and must frame roadmap dates as targets, not contractual guarantees [NL-009#NL-009-S08].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
